  "verbalization": "Russujaponol A appears to interact with HEp-2 through a series of molecular targets, all of which are involved in the synthesis of nucleic acids. The drug's mechanism of action is mediated through GMP synthase [glutamine-hydrolyzing], which is targeted by multiple compounds, including Notoamide P, Methyl 8-Hydroxy-2,2-Dimethylchromene-6-Carboxylate, and Dragmacidin E. These compounds, in turn, target HEp-2, suggesting a potential pathway where Russujaponol A may exert its effects by modulating the activity of GMP synthase, thereby influencing cellular processes in the HEp-2 cell line. The consistent targeting of GMP synthase across different compounds implies a shared functional role in the drug's mechanism, although the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence supports a plausible link between Russujaponol A and HEp-2, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the precise molecular mechanism.",
